WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.934
Welcome, welcome, welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:05.300
You're here. Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.801
Oh, awesome. -Happy birthday!

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:08.734
-Thank you. I appreciate it. Thank you.

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:10.601
It's my birthday. Thank you very much.

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:14.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:17.200
You know, it's funny. I forgot how old I am.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.234
'Cause you reach a certain age and you forgot how old you are.

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:22.534
It just happens. So I go -- Yeah, I'm, uh...

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:25.901
You know, I'm 49 or whatever, you know.

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:28.534
And so that's great. The card's -- "You're 49."

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:30.367
I go, "I don't think I'm 49, am I?"

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:32.167
And they go, "Yeah, yeah, you are."

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:33.434
And so my daughter goes,

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:35.300
"Alexa, how old is Jimmy Fallon?"

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:40.167
Alexa -- "Jimmy Fallon is 48 years old."

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:42.868
It's like -- "That's the best gift ever!"

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:45.300
You gave me a year of my life back!

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.267
I have a whole year ahead of me for free!

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:50.734
Let's get to some news, you guys.

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:52.234
Last night, President Biden

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:54.167
did a rare sit-down interview on "60 Minutes."

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:55.334
I don't know if you saw this.

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:56.567
And he made a pretty big announcement.

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:57.968
In case you missed it, here it is.

00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:00.100
-Is the pandemic over?

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.234
-The pandemic is over.

00:01:02.234 --> 00:01:04.100
We still have a problem with COVID.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.667
We're still doing a lot of work on it.

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:08.834
It's -- But the pandemic is over.

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:16.300
-It's kind of huge news to mention so casually, you know?

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.868
I wasn't expecting the end of a two-and-a-half-year nightmare

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:21.834
to be announced on the floor of the Detroit Auto Show.

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:24.667
It's like hearing, "I had a good day.

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:29.634
Went for a run, ate breakfast, the baby was born, you know."

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:31.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:34.534
Apparently Biden's comment was not part of his planned remarks

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:37.834
and caught several of his own health officials by surprise.

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:39.334
Dr. Fauci was like, "Oh, God.

00:01:39.334 --> 00:01:41.400
it's 2020 all over again. Oh, my God."

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.968
For the rest of the interview,

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:44.467
whenever Biden answered a question,

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:46.100
a staffer quickly revved a car engine.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.567
He's like, "That's right. We're going to go to war with Ch--"

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.601
[ Engine revs, tires screech ]

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:51.868
"We're gonna support Tai--"

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:53.901
[ Engine revs, tires screech ]

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:56.634
Later in the interview, Biden, though, was asked about his age.

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:58.000
Watch this.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.200
-Mr. President, you are the oldest president ever.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.834
-Pretty good shape, huh?

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:05.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:07.901
[ Applause ]

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:10.767
-He handled it pretty well, yeah.

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.834
Although, I will say it got a little dicey after that.

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:14.100
Take a look at this.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.934
-How would you say your mental focus is?

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:19.734
-Oh, it's focused. [ Laughs ]

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.968
I say -- I think it's -- I -- I haven't -- Look.

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:24.000
You think I would tell you if I knew exactly?

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.667
Of course I'm not going to tell you.

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:28.868
So I -- Look. This is a process.

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:30.200
This is a process.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.901
And the proof of the pudding's in the eating.

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:37.167
I mean, don't -- don't -- don't.

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:41.167
My point is, it takes time. How's an old guy do that?

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:43.834
I no more think of myself as being as old as I am

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.534
than a fly.

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:46.667
-What do you mean?

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:48.234
-No.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.367
-No, man. Yo, yo, yo. Yo!

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:51.934
-That's edited, right?

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:54.834
-No. -Alright. Thank you.

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:57.434
-That's a joke. -No, that's not real.

00:02:57.434 --> 00:02:58.567
-Oh God.

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:00.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:03.100
-Props to our editors there.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.634
Well, I saw that this weekend

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:07.534
former president Trump spoke at a rally in Ohio,

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:08.901
and at one point during his speech,

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:10.434
music started playing,

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:12.133
and his supporters reacted in a pretty strange way.

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:13.534
Check this out.

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:16.200
-And a Department of Justice that refuses to investigate

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.567
egregious acts... [ Grand, sweeping music plays ]

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:21.534
...of voting irregularities and fraud.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:25.567
And we have a president who is cognitively impaired

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:29.133
and in no condition to lead our country.

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:31.400
-Not creepy at all.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.434
Then Trump was like,

00:03:33.434 --> 00:03:35.934
"And now to sacrifice the first-born sons.

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:38.234
Come up here, Don Jr."

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:40.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:42.267
What was going on?

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:44.400
Meanwhile, Trump just returned to Mar-a-lago

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.667
for the first time since the FBI search,

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:49.200
and he's complaining that FBI agents

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:53.067
didn't even take off their shoes before going into his bedroom.

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:55.033
Yeah, for some reason,

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:57.167
the agents weren't like, "FBI! This is a raid!"

00:03:57.167 --> 00:04:00.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.434 --> 00:04:03.234
"Should have wore Velcro."

00:04:03.234 --> 00:04:04.767
Of course, everyone is talking about this today --

00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:06.334
leaders, dignitaries, and politicians

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.367
from around the world gathered in London

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:10.033
for the funeral of Queen Elizabeth.

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:12.000
Meanwhile, Trump showed up at a Burger King

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.834
and said, "Sorry for your loss."

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:16.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:21.033
"Two whoppers. French fries. Diet Coke."

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:23.801
[ Applause ]

00:04:23.801 --> 00:04:25.868
In observance for the funeral,

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:28.334
flights in and out of London's Heathrow Airport

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.567
were canceled or delayed.

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:32.133
LaGuardia heard that and was like,

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:35.167
"Uh, that's also why our flights are, uh..."

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:38.000
[ Clears throat ] "Out of respect, of course.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.634
We're gonna be respecting till, like,

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:41.601
around New Year's, probably. That's what was...

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:43.868
We'll continue our respect. Yeah."

00:04:43.868 --> 00:04:46.200
Some entertainment news -- we're just one month away

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:47.901
from the release of Taylor Swift's

00:04:47.901 --> 00:04:49.601
10th studio album, "Midnights."

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:52.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:56.100
And fans are already finding all kinds of secret messages

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.133
about the album in her social-media posts.

00:04:58.133 --> 00:05:01.100
-Oh, man, all that stuff is just conspiracy theories, though.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.601
-Uh, I don't know, Tariq. The clues are --

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:05.868
The clues are everywhere. -What clues?

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:07.734
-Okay, so, Taylor made a surprise announcement

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:09.667
at this year's VMAs that her 10th studio album

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:10.968
was gonna be called "Midnights"

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:13.501
and it would come out at midnight on October 21st.

00:05:13.501 --> 00:05:15.200
You follow? -Uh...

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.334
-So, 13 is Taylor's favorite number,

00:05:17.334 --> 00:05:19.267
and "Midnights" is gonna have 13 tracks on it,

00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:21.234
but nobody knows what the songs are called yet.

00:05:21.234 --> 00:05:22.968
On all the album art she's shared so far,

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:24.467
all the songs have fake titles

00:05:24.467 --> 00:05:26.601
like "Track One," "Track Two," that kind of thing.

00:05:26.601 --> 00:05:29.267
-And that means...? -But when she posted a video

00:05:29.267 --> 00:05:31.534
announcing all of the limited-edition vinyls,

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:33.734
the names of the songs were all blurred out on the covers,

00:05:33.734 --> 00:05:35.200
so you can tell the songs won't actually be called

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.267
"Track One," "Track Two." And that was on September 1st.

00:05:37.267 --> 00:05:38.734
Then on September 16th,

00:05:38.734 --> 00:05:40.167
she posted another video revealing

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:43.334
that if you line up the backs of all the special-edition vinyls

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:46.000
with the regular-edition one, it makes a clock.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.033
Midnight is a time on a clock.

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:51.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:51.634 --> 00:05:53.767
-Okay. Okay, well, I guess -- -Yeah, but here --

00:05:53.767 --> 00:05:55.367
here's where it gets interesting.

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:57.634
In Taylor's entire discography,

00:05:57.634 --> 00:06:00.133
she's only sung the word "midnight" in six songs.

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:02.167
She sings it in "Style" off of "1989,"

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:03.567
"You Are in Love" off of "1989,"

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:05.000
"New Year's Day" off of "Reputation,"

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.667
"The Last Great American Dynasty" off "Folklore,"

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:08.000
"Happiness" off of "Evermore,"

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.601
and, of course, in "22 (Taylor's Version)"

00:06:09.601 --> 00:06:10.868
off "Red (Taylor's Version)."

00:06:10.868 --> 00:06:12.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.234 --> 00:06:13.901
And that's not even the crazy part.

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:16.601
'Cause it also turns out she's sung the phrase "middle of the night"

00:06:16.601 --> 00:06:18.434
in seven songs throughout her discography.

00:06:18.434 --> 00:06:20.534
She sings it in "...Ready For It?" off "Reputation,"

00:06:20.534 --> 00:06:21.767
"Daylight" off of "Lover,"

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:23.100
"You Belong with Me (Taylor's Version)"

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:24.534
off of "Fearless (Taylor's Version),"

00:06:24.534 --> 00:06:25.667
"Untouchable (Taylor's Version),"

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:26.968
off of "Fearless (Taylor's Version),"

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:28.767
"All Too Well (10 Minute Version) (Taylor's Version)"

00:06:28.767 --> 00:06:30.300
off of "Red (Taylor's Version),"

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.501
"Better Man (Taylor's Version)"

00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:33.033
off of "Red (Taylor's Version),"

00:06:33.033 --> 00:06:35.267
and "Nothing New (feat. Phoebe Bridgers) (Taylor's version)"

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:36.934
off of "Red (Taylor's Version)."

00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:40.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.067
-What are you even saying?!

00:06:42.067 --> 00:06:45.167
-Six "midnights" plus seven "middle of the nights"

00:06:45.167 --> 00:06:47.501
equal...13.

00:06:47.501 --> 00:06:49.400
13 is Taylor's favorite number.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.367
That's how many songs are on "Midnights."

00:06:51.367 --> 00:06:52.901
Taylor's a genius!

00:06:52.901 --> 00:06:55.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:55.367 --> 00:06:57.167
That's what.

00:06:57.167 --> 00:06:59.300
You get it now? -Yeah, I get it.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:02.067
Happy birthday. -Thank you. I appreciate it.

00:07:02.067 --> 00:07:03.601
Well, this is going viral.

00:07:03.601 --> 00:07:06.901
Guys, an 80-year-old state Senate candidate in Utah

00:07:06.901 --> 00:07:08.767
